{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/outDegree(of:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"outDegree"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L275","fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift"},"role":"symbol","title":"outDegree(of:)","extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"outDegree"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V9outDegree2ofS2i_tF","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/outdegree(of:)"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of columns with "},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" among their sources. O(1), cached."}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","abstract":[{"text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/Oriented